# Environment Configuration Example

## Backend (.env)

```env
# Server
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=5000
HOST=localhost

# Database
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=android_remote_hub
DB_USER=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=your_password_here

# Authentication
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_here_min_32_chars_long
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=your_refresh_secret_here_min_32_chars
JWT_EXPIRY=1h
JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRY=7d

# Encryption
ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_32_char_hex_key_here

# CORS
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Logging
LOG_LEVEL=debug

# File Upload
UPLOAD_DIR=./uploads
MAX_FILE_SIZE=104857600
```

## Dashboard (.env)

```env
# API Configuration
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:5000
VITE_APP_NAME=Android Remote Hub
```

## Production (Railway)

### Backend
```env
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=5000
DB_HOST=<railway-provided-host>
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=<database-name>
DB_USER=<database-user>
DB_PASSWORD=<strong-password>
JWT_SECRET=<generate-with-crypto>
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=<generate-with-crypto>
ENCRYPTION_KEY=<32-char-hex-key>
CORS_ORIGIN=https://<your-domain>.railway.app
LOG_LEVEL=info
```

### Dashboard
```env
VITE_API_URL=https://<backend-url>.railway.app
VITE_WS_URL=wss://<backend-url>.railway.app
VITE_APP_NAME=Android Remote Hub
```

## Generate Secrets

```bash
# Generate 32-char JWT Secret
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"

# Generate 16-char Encryption Key (32-char hex)
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(16).toString('hex'))"

# Verify key length
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(16).toString('hex').length)"
```

## Database Setup

```bash
# Connect to PostgreSQL
psql -U postgres

# Create database
CREATE DATABASE android_remote_hub;

# Create user
CREATE USER arh_user WITH PASSWORD 'your_strong_password';

# Grant privileges
ALTER ROLE arh_user SET client_encoding TO 'utf8';
ALTER ROLE arh_user SET default_transaction_isolation TO 'read committed';
ALTER ROLE arh_user SET default_transaction_deferrable TO on;
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE android_remote_hub TO arh_user;

# Exit
\q
```

## Railway Deployment

1. Connect GitHub repo to Railway
2. Add PostgreSQL service
3. Copy DATABASE_URL from PostgreSQL service
4. Set all variables in backend service settings
5. Set dashboard variables
6. Deploy!

## Security Notes

⚠️ **NEVER** commit .env files
⚠️ **ALWAYS** use strong, random secrets in production
⚠️ **ROTATE** secrets regularly
⚠️ **USE** HTTPS/WSS in production
⚠️ **VALIDATE** all environment variables on startup
